    "created_at": "2020-11-04T16:07:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-04T16:07:54Z",
    "body": "> If you put it at (a), it would make the main element not be a [hierarchically correct main element ](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/dev/grouping-content.html#hierarchically-correct-main-element) and therefore invalid.\r\n\r\nok I agree with (a) being incorrect there.\r\n\r\nwhat about (b)? main is not sectioning content but it hasn't been stated as needing an explicit section element anywhere in the specs. that I could find...\r\n\r\nI think it might be better for the main element to be sectioning content to avoid the explicit section element required by semantics.\r\nlike the main element examples in the spec:\r\n[1](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/dev/grouping-content.html#the-main-element:the-main-element-4) and [2](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/dev/grouping-content.html#the-main-element:the-main-element-5)",
