    "created_at": "2020-11-05T01:47:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-11-05T01:49:12Z",
    "body": "The main element examples in the spec don't use multiple unhidden h1 elements. The h1 elements start implicit sections so it's really down to the intent of the second h1 element, not the main element. If the second h1 is intended to end the section headed by the first h1 (which is started by the sectioning-root body element) and start a new section at the same level, then there shouldn't be section element around it. If the second h1 is intended to start a subsection of the section headed by the first h1, then it would be necessary to surround it with a sectioning element, or to change the h1 to an h2 element.. If the former of these,  then (b) would be the appropriate place. But this would be exactly the same if the main element wasn't present.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
